<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sharkha Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1300 CE – 1450 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Muslim principality of the south-eastern Ethiopian highlands, listed among the seven Muslim states of medieval Abyssinia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sharkha is known almost only from the 14th-century Arab geographer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-umari">al-Umari</a>, who named it among the seven Muslim kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Abyssinia</a>. It probably lay in the Arsi highlands, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hadiya-sultanate">Hadiya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bale">Bale</a>, in a region of farming and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> herding settled by Muslim communities along the trade routes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-umari">Al-Umari</a> describes it as a modest state with a small army, whose people grew crops and kept livestock. After the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amda-seyon-i">Amda Seyon</a> in the 1330s it paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>, though its local Muslim rulers kept their positions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sharkha fades from the record in the 15th century. Its lands were later caught up in the wars of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> and then settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> groups during the migrations of the 16th century.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1300 CE – 1450 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.57%;width:2.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1300 CE – 1450 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sharkha, Sharka</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1375&amp;focus=sharkha-sultanate" aria-label="Sharkha Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5754 1865 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sharkha Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6029 1964h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6074 2121h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6074 2121h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ethiopia. <a href="/atlas?year=1375&amp;focus=sharkha-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

